  "what_for": "post5 plus an int8 P.V twin of the flows' tuned kernel (round K): the same q / k quantisation, Q.K^T and online softmax as qk_int8_sv_f16_accum_f16_attn_inst_buf_sc3d, then P as u8 relative to each 64-key block's maximum (round(P * 255)) times v as s8 per 64-token block and channel (mean subtracted) on the int8 tensor cores (mma m16n8k32 u8.s8 -> s32), scaled into fp32 accumulators by pmax / 255 per row and v's scale per channel; the denominator from the fp32 P; v's mean added after the normalisation. A different rounding than the fp16 op (emulated first: round K's emulate.py variant u8-blk-m-lf); every kernel of post5 is unchanged",
